-- title:
--   X Evaluated Full Slice ABABtensor To Evaluated Slice ABABAvg
-- statement:
--   **The x-evaluated full-slice tensor endpoint reaches the evaluated-slice quartic.**
--
--   Let $(q,m,d)$ have a field model, let $S$ be a symmetric strategy on the successor space, and let `family` be a slice-indexed polynomial submeasurement family. Assume that the state is normalized and that `family` is strongly self-consistent in $S$ with error $\zeta$. Then the x-evaluated full-slice $\mathrm{ABAB}$ tensor average is within the explicit sampling and self-consistency error of the evaluated-slice scalar quartic:
--
--   $$
--   \left|
--   \mathrm{xEvaluatedFullSliceABABtensorAvg}(S,\mathrm{family})
--   -\mathrm{evaluatedSliceABABAvg}(S,\mathrm{family})
--   \right|
--   \le \frac{m d}{q}+\sqrt{\zeta}.
--   $$
--
--   This is the y-tail bridge in the full-slice transport argument. It is used by `fullSlice_scalar_marginalize_y` to replace the tensor endpoint by the evaluated-slice average.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Commutativity.xEvaluatedFullSliceABABtensor_to_evaluatedSliceABABAvg`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
